{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Every artifact that bears on this trip describes one and the same trip: EV-TRIP-00519, EV-GPS-00519 and EV-FARE-00519 all carry trip_id TRP-00519, the trace's first fix at 08:06:40+08:00 matches trip_record.started_at, and all three are admitted at weight_multiplier 1.0 with an empty issues list. The rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08 as to identity is therefore discharged, and no admitted artifact contradicts her account of the ride.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00519", "EV-GPS-00519", "EV-FARE-00519"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's route instruction satisfies POL-RD-04 on its face. It came from the rider (limb (a)); it was sent at 08:08:10+08:00, ninety seconds after the trip started at 08:06:40+08:00, so it precedes any departure from the corridor (limb (b)); and it does not say 'go the fast way' or 'you know better' — it names roads, 'take Clementi Rd then North Buona Vista', which is specific enough to act on (limb (c)). It is exactly the kind of instruction the clause treats as actionable, not a vague passenger wish the driver may brush aside.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00519", "EV-TRIP-00519"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's silence is carried by an artifact, not by assertion. EV-CHAT-00519 records exactly two messages for the whole trip, both from the rider — MSG-00519-001 at 08:08:10 and MSG-00519-002 'hello?' at 08:10:40 — each marked delivered and read before the next was sent, and not one message from the driver, in a chat the trip_record confirms ran to two messages. Any account that cites no artifact to the contrary carries no weight under POL-RD-08, so the rider's account that the driver refused to explain or discuss is the only account of the exchange on the record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00519", "EV-TRIP-00519"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-01 makes the trace the governing measurement, and on EV-GPS-00519 the vehicle covered 2.71 km against a booked optimal of 5.0 km — an excess of -2.29 km, derived excess_pct -45.8%, derived status 'no deviation'. The rider therefore does not press a POL-RD-02 distance recomputation, which on these numbers would yield nothing; her case is that she received roughly 46% less of the booked journey than she was charged for, after her written instruction was left unanswered.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00519", "EV-TRIP-00519"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing in the pool can exculpate the driver's route choice. The only traffic advisory linked to this trip, EV-ADVIS-00519-01, is MISSING — weight_multiplier 0.0, blocking issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, detail 'No advisory covers the optimal corridor in this window' — and that impairment is disclosed here as POL-GEN-02 requires. Under POL-GEN-02(3) the absence is itself citable while it can carry no fact, and under POL-RD-03 an advisory that does not exist cannot exculpate any corridor decision; so no closure, contraflow or other external event explains the route or the silence.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00519-01", "EV-GPS-00519"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider is not the claimant POL-RD-08 guards against: rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 0 and rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0, so the enhanced-corroboration condition (four or more claims with one or fewer substantiated) is not engaged and no corroboration beyond the gps_trace is required of her. These are the two profile fields POL-RD-08 names and they are cited for that test alone, as POL-GEN-01 requires; no other profile field on either party is relied on here.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00519"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "With fare_breakdown.payment_status at CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd at 0.00 (EV-FARE-00519), a NO_ACTION leaves the rider carrying the entire disputed 9.99 for a trip whose central question — whether the driver's route and his refusal to answer a plainly stated instruction were justified — rests on nothing the record can test: the sole advisory is absent at weight 0.0, chat_message.waypoint_hint is null, and no road-level fact is derived from the trace. That is the situation POL-RD-10 addresses, and its limb (7) applies: the two accounts are of comparable strength and the deciding fact is carried by no artifact. The rider asks that the amount be held for human review rather than collected from her — under POL-GEN-03 an escalated amount is held, not collected, and under POL-RD-10 the rider is not left paying in full on an unanswered record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00519", "EV-CHAT-00519", "EV-GPS-00519", "EV-ADVIS-00519-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this was a metered trip (TRP-00519) from The Clementi Mall, and the rider alighted early at Commonwealth Ave W; SGD 9.99 was charged.\n\nThe route-deviation test in POL-RD-01 compares the distance actually driven with the booked optimal route. The governing measurement is the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00519, weight 1.0): 2.71 km against a booked optimal of 5.0 km (EV-TRIP-00519, weight 1.0). That is an excess of -2.29 km (-45.8%) — a shortfall, not an excess. Both establishment tests require an excess greater than 20% of the optimal route AND greater than 0.8 km; neither can pass on a negative figure. No deviation is established, and POL-RD-01 directs NO_ACTION however the trip felt to the rider.\n\nThe trace is whole — 73 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps, maximum gap 0.0 s — so the POL-RD-07(a)-(c) impairment limbs are not met and the 2.71 km trace figure governs over the rounded 2.7 km convenience copy on the trip record.\n\nThe fare arithmetic points the same way. Recomputed on the booked optimal route under POL-RD-02, the fare would be SGD 10.87 (base SGD 3.80 + 0.75 × 5.0 km + 0.28 × 9 min + SGD 0.80 platform fee) against SGD 9.99 actually charged, so the refund floors at zero and is de minimis in any event: the rider paid less than the optimal route would have cost. There are no ERP gantry lines and no airport surcharge, so POL-RD-09 yields no separate pass-through or billing-integrity correction, and nothing can be added to a zero distance refund.\n\nThe rider's request for a full refund rests on the driver's silence. I accept the account in EV-CHAT-00519: two rider messages (08:08:10 asking for Clementi Rd and North Buona Vista, and 08:10:40 'hello?'), delivered and read, with no reply from the driver, consistent with EV-TRIP-00519's chat_message_count of 2. I also accept the rider's POL-RD-04 point that the instruction was specific enough to act on. But a communication grievance is not a route deviation, and this policy attaches no money to it in this category; and because the rider alighted early, no excess distance exists for POL-RD-04 to exonerate. No driver compensation arises under POL-RD-04 either: the fare billed 2.7 km against a 2.71 km trace, a shortfall of 0.01 km, far below the 1.0 km threshold.\n\nOn the driver's side, the identity and burden points under POL-RD-08 are accepted (all artifacts carry TRP-00519, and no excess meets the POL-RD-01 threshold from the unimpaired trace), and the POL-RD-01/POL-RD-07 trace-integrity point is accepted. The only traffic advisory for this trip, EV-ADVIS-00519-01, is MISSING at weight 0.0 (issue MISSING_ARTIFACT); its absence cannot exculpate any corridor decision, and nothing turns on it because no deviation exists. The POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is not engaged — there is no material deviation and no pattern (deviation_flags_90d 0 over 250 completed trips in 90 days) — so no driver-conduct referral arises. The rider-profile fields cited under POL-RD-08 (deviation_claims_60d 0, deviation_claims_60d_substantiated 0) do not engage enhanced corroboration.\n\nOutcome: NO_ACTION. POL-GEN-03 leaves the present state as it is — payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00 are unchanged. No POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires: the trace is unimpaired, all identifiers and timestamps on the admitted artifacts agree, the exculpatory clauses are not invoked against anything missing, and no charge line lacks a counterpart. Confidence rests on the deciding facts being carried by artifacts at full weight (EV-GPS-00519, EV-TRIP-00519, EV-FARE-00519, all 1.0). If the rider wants the driver's non-response reviewed as a service-quality matter, that is a legitimate concern but it is not a matter this category's money rules address, and no clause here produces a referral for it."
  },
