    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both of you agree on the central fact, and the record confirms it: the vehicle did not travel a longer route than the platform's optimal route. The governing GPS trace (EV-GPS-00519) measures the ride at 2.71 km against a booked optimal of 5.0 km (EV-TRIP-00519) — an excess of −2.29 km, or −45.8%. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only where the excess is greater than 20% of the optimal distance AND greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms; a negative excess fails both tests, and the clause directs NO_ACTION however the trip is characterised, save for a billing-integrity correction under POL-RD-09(4). The trace used for that measure is unimpaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 — 73 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps, maximum gap 0.0 seconds — so its 2.71 km reading governs over the rounded 2.7 km convenience copy on the trip record.\n\nTo the rider: I accept your account of the exchange. EV-CHAT-00519 records a specific, timely instruction ('take Clementi Rd then North Buona Vista, fewer lights') sent at 08:08:10, ninety seconds after the trip started, and two messages from you with none from the driver, so the driver's silence is carried by an artifact rather than assertion. But a communication grievance is not a route deviation, and this policy gives no monetary remedy for it. The reason the drive was short is also on the record: the trip_record dropoff is labelled 'Commonwealth Ave W, rider alighted early' and the trip ended at 08:18:40. A journey cut short by the passenger produces a shortfall, not an excess, and POL-RD-01 measures excess only. Your named-road instruction is specific enough to act on, but because there is no excess to exonerate, POL-RD-04 changes nothing here — there is simply no deviation to excuse or to charge.\n\nOn the money: POL-RD-02 recomputes the optimal-route fare at SGD 10.87 (base 3.80 + 0.75 × 5.0 km = 3.75 + 0.28 × 9.0 min = 2.52 + 0.80 platform fee) against a charged total of SGD 9.99 (EV-FARE-00519). Charged minus recomputed is negative, so the refund floors at zero and sits below the SGD 0.50 de-minimis line in any event; you in fact paid less than the optimal route would have cost. The fare that was charged matches the ride actually taken (2.70 km and 12 minutes at the rate card, 9.99 total). There are no ERP gantries, no airport surcharge and no promotional lines, so the standalone pass-through and billing-integrity corrections under POL-RD-09, including limb (4), are unavailable and nothing can be added on top of a zero distance refund.\n\nThe traffic advisory linked to this trip (EV-ADVIS-00519-01) is missing, weight 0.0, with the MISSING_ARTIFACT issue; its absence is citable but it can carry no fact and exonerates no corridor. No exoneration is needed in any event, because no deviation exists.\n\nThe profiles play no part in the outcome, as POL-GEN-01 requires. The driver's trailing-90-day deviation flags are zero (0 of 250 completed trips), so no repeat-pattern uplift or POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arises; the rider's deviation-claims counters are zero, so no enhanced corroboration under POL-RD-08 is required. No trigger under POL-RD-10 fires — the trip identifiers match, the timestamps do not disagree, the trace is unimpaired, and there is no pass-through line lacking a counterpart — so this is decided on the evidence rather than escalated.\n\nOutcome for both parties: NO_ACTION. The charge of SGD 9.99 stands, no refund issues, and fare_breakdown.payment_status remains CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd at 0.00."
  },
